From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abue Ammar <14371506+abue-ammar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:59:04 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Narrow File Search to home with editable defaults (#1625)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* Narrow File Search to home with editable defaults

Adding a folder under the default `/` scope did nothing: normalizing
folded it into `/` and dropped it from the list. The list now keeps what
the user adds; only the crawl folds a nested scope.

The default scope is home, and the ignore list is one stored list seeded
with recommended defaults — build and dependency folders, the Photos
library, the Trash, tool caches and the noisy parts of ~/Library. Every
row can be removed, and Restore Defaults brings either list back.

* Keep shipped ignore rules compiled in, stored as edits

Storing the whole ignore list let a value saved by an earlier build, in
UserDefaults, settings.json or a backup, replace the new defaults with
the user's additions alone, or with nothing. The shipped rules are
compiled in again; fileSearchIgnorePatterns keeps only what the user
added, and the new fileSearchRemovedDefaultPatterns the rules they
removed. Restore Defaults clears both.

/Library/Caches and /private/var/folders return to the defaults so a
scope of / stays filtered.
